   Parts of the training and inference code were adapted from
   rv_train/models/qwen/model.py and rv_train/train.py:
     - clap/utils.py: system prompt, chat formatting (format_data), action
       discretization (actions_to_text / text_to_actions), image tiling, and
       action-token mask augmentation (apply_action_mask_aug). Rewritten as
       standalone functions; the system prompt is extended with the CLAP
       <think> language-action prefix.
     - clap/train.py: training-loop design (label masking, LR scaled by the
       number of GPUs). Re-implemented with DDP, gradient accumulation and
       trackio logging.
     - clap/policy.py: inference (image preprocessing, prompting, generation
       and parsing of the integer action sequence), re-implemented for
       batched CLAP inference.

   eval/eval.py is an independent implementation that follows the LIBERO
   evaluation protocol of VLA-0 (roboverse/evals/libero/eval.py), which in
   turn comes from the LIBERO example of openpi
   (https://github.com/Physical-Intelligence/openpi): environment resolution,
   dummy-action warm-up, camera flip and the per-suite maximum episode
   lengths. Its batched design (vectorized LIBERO environments with one
   batched generate() call per step) is inspired by RLinf
   (https://github.com/RLinf/RLinf).

